                <pb facs="0284" n="250" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg250"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sherman to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-05-21"><hi rendition="#italic">May 21,
                        1897</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Admiral Joseph N. Miller will represent the Navy and Gen. Nelson A. Miles the
                    Army, and the President will send two eminent civilians to act as
                    representatives of our Government at the ceremonial of the Jubilee. All will be
                    associated with you as a special embassy, you being its head. Instructions will
                    follow as soon as details can be settled.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sherman.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
